  "description": "An equal star count separates nothing, so the boundary falls through to approval",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Tally: 'Each rule ranks and narrows the tied set; whatever remains tied falls through to the next rule. A rule that separates nothing is skipped.' Phase 1 / Selecting finalists: the same chain, with star_votes at rung 2.",
  "rationale": "N_FINALISTS is 2, 5 attendees. m1: 5 rows (u1-u4 yes, u5 no) -> coverage 1.00, yes 4, approval 0.80, stars 0 -> slot 1. m2: 3 rows (u1 yes STARRED, u2 yes, u3 no) -> coverage 0.60, yes 2, approval 2/3 = 0.6667, star_votes 1. m3: 4 rows (u1 yes STARRED, u2 yes, u3 no, u4 no) -> coverage 0.80, yes 2, approval 2/4 = 0.50, star_votes 1. All eligible, all clearing APPROVAL_FLOOR. m2 and m3 tie on yes-votes (2 each) for the last slot, AND tie on star_votes (1 each). The star rung therefore separates nothing and is skipped -- it does not become the deciding rule and does not narrow by id -- so rung 3 decides: approval 0.6667 > 0.50 -> m2 admitted, m3 excluded, decided at the boundary by 'approval'. Runoff over {m1, m2}: m1 preferred 3 (u1, u2, u3) to 2 (u4, u5) -> Condorcet winner.",
